ZVSE2

; Combat_BattleShadows example. Put this file into the Data\s folder of your mod.

; Example 1 (on): a shadow that follows the mouse by itself, as fast as the Fireball shadow.
;   P(radius)/(contour): radius 0..4 (0 = only the mouse hex), -1 = off; contour 1 = blinking blue outline.
;   It stays on until switched off with -1 or until the next battle action, so calling it on every hint is fine.
!?MM0;
!!FU(BattleShadow_Follow):P1/1;

; Example 2 (off): a shape built from the hint position. Removed by the plugin when the next MM0 starts.
; To turn it on, replace the first character * with ! on the next three lines.
*?MM0;
*!MM:D?(hex:y);
*!FU(BattleShadow_Radius):P(hex)/1/1;

; Example 3 (off): free shape, up to 10 hexes. -1 = empty slot. The 11th value is the contour switch.
*?MM0;
*!FU(BattleShadow_Hexes):P52/53/54/71/-1/-1/-1/-1/-1/-1/1;

; Diagnostics (off): shows the plugin state in the battle hint line instead of the normal hint.
*!FU(BattleShadow_Debug):P?y20/?y21/?y22/?y23/?y24/?y25/?y26/?y27/?y28;
*!MM:M^v%y20 painted=%y21 hint=%y22 follow=%y23 noShade=%y24 option=%y25 repaints=%y26 anchor=%y27 cursor=%y28^;
